    "intro_narrative": "You awaken in the sealed laboratory of Professor Gearwick, surrounded by hissing pipes, turning cogs, and the suffocating heat of trapped steam. The heavy brass door is locked tight, and the pressure in the room is slowly rising. The only way out is to activate his master invention: the linguistic difference engine. You must trace the flow of data through his array of steam-powered analytical machines, decrypters, and punch-card readers. Follow the mechanical logic, deduce the connections between the various gear-driven devices, and power up the final engine before the boiler overloads completely.",
    "narrative_style": "steampunk"
  },
